<!-- Author: Christina Safranski                                           -->

<!--
<section name = "exercise-1-1-d-1"><title>Title here</title>
  <statement>
-->

<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to="6"/>
  <function name="f" >($a^x-1)/x</function>
  
</setup>
<p> 
  Notice that if we try to determine <m>\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0} \frac{$a^x-1}{x}</m> by simply letting <m>x \to 0</m>, we get <m>\frac{0}{0}</m>, which is called an <q>indeterminate form</q> (literally: <q>we don't yet know</q>) and so we need to do more work to find the limit's value.
</p>
<p>
  Observe that none of our usual algebraic techniques apply here, since there's not an operation we can perform to get the <m>x</m> out of the exponent in <m>4^x</m>.  Instead, we do some numerical approximation.
</p>
<p>
  Fill in the following table to see how the function is behaving for several values near <m>x=0</m>. Enter your answers as decimals, with at least 4 places after the decimal point.
</p>
<tabular top="minor" bottom="minor" left="minor" right="minor">
    <row header>
      <cell><m>x</m></cell>
      <cell><m>\frac{$a^x-1}{x}</m></cell>
    </row>
   <row>
      <cell><m>-0.1</m></cell>
     <cell><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>$$f(-0.1)</number></answer></cell>
   </row>
  <row>
      <cell><m>-0.01</m></cell>
    <cell><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>$$f(-0.01)</number></answer></cell>
  </row>
  <row>
      <cell><m>-0.001</m></cell>
     <cell><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>$$f(-0.001)</number></answer></cell>
  </row>
  <row>
      <cell><m>0</m></cell>
     <cell><mathInput disabled></mathInput></cell>
  </row>
  <row>
      <cell><m>0.001</m></cell>
    <cell><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>$$f(0.001)</number></answer></cell>
  </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>0.01</m></cell>
    <cell><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>$$f(0.01)</number></answer></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>0.1</m></cell>
      <cell><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>$$f(0.1)</number></answer></cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>
<p>
 Using the table of values to guide you, what do you expect is the value of the limit as <m>x\to 0</m>?  
</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle\lim_{x\to 0} \frac{$a^x-1}{x}</m>= <answer name="limans" symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.0001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number>ln($a)</number></answer>
</p>